{"tool_name":"omia","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"omia","home":"http://omia.angis.org.au/home/","license":"Not licensed","summary":"A catalogue/compendium of inherited disorders, other (single-locus) traits, and genes in 233 animal species (other than human and mouse and rats, which have their own resources).","addition_date":"2017-08-20T16:31:52Z","last_update_date":"2020-01-19T17:47:47Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:omia","credit":[{"email":"frank.nicholas@sydney.edu.au","name":"Frank Nicholas","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://omia.org/home/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"}]}],"name":"OMIA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkj152","metadata":{"abstract":"Online Mendelian Inheritance in Animals (OMIA) is a comprehensive, annotated catalogue of inherited disorders and other familial traits in animals other than humans and mice. Structured as a comparative biology resource, OMIA is a comprehensive resource of phenotypic information on heritable animal traits and genes in a strongly comparative context, relating traits to genes where possible. OMIA is modelled on and is complementary to Online Mendelian Inheritance in Man (OMIM). OMIA has been moved to a MySQL database at the Australian National Genomic Information Service (ANGIS) and can be accessed at http://omia.angis.org.au/. It has also been integrated into the Entrez search interface at the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI; http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?db=omia). Curation of OMIA data by researchers working on particular species and diso